[Term]
id: CLCO:0000057
name: clinical association
def: "A reified assertion relating two or more clinical entities, representing a contextualized clinical statement that can carry qualifiers such as negation, uncertainty, and temporality." []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES: \"The patient has pneumonia\", \"The MRI showed a mass\", and \"Surgery was recommended\" are clinical associations.\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES: patient, pneumonia, and severe are entities or values, not associations by themselves.\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: The first statement expresses a has finding association, the second a has finding association, and the third a recommendation association." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Although these structures represent relationships between clinical entities, we model them as reified associations rather than relations, because they represent contextualized assertions with additional attributes (e.g., negation, uncertainty, temporality), which cannot be expressed using binary object properties in OWL.\nThese relations include the most frequently documented relation types as defined in:\nColicchio, Tiago K., Pavithra I. Dissanayake, and James J. Cimino. \"Formal representation of patients’ care context data: the path to improving the electronic health record.\" Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association 27, no. 11 (2020): 1648-1657." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "CLCO represents temporal information through four orthogonal mechanisms: (1) temporal_frame (qualifier axis) -- document-relative context via has_temporal_frame, values historical/current/future/hypothetical; (2) completion_status (qualifier axis) -- workflow state via has_completion_status, values pending/in_progress/completed; (3) datatype time properties (data axis) -- computable timestamps via has_start_time, has_end_time, has_duration_value with xsd typed literals; (4) reified temporal associations (entity axis) -- narrative temporal entities such as has_onset, has_date, has_duration where the temporal expression is a first-class clinical_entity linked via has_object. These mechanisms are independent: a single association may carry values from any combination." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000058
name: has setting
def: "Inference about the location or setting where a clinical event happened." []
xref: OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:32462
is_a: CLCO:0000057 ! clinical association
intersection_of: CLCO:0000057 ! clinical association
intersection_of: CLCO:0002501 CLCO:0000107 ! has object setting
relationship: CLCO:0002501 CLCO:0000107 ! has object setting
property_value: IAO:0000112 "He was given Zofran and meclizine at Urgent Care." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"in the emergency department\" => has setting\n\"at home\" => has setting\n\"in the intensive care unit\" => has setting\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"chest pain\" => finding, NOT has setting\n\"tomorrow\" => has date, NOT has setting\n\"physician\" => clinician, NOT has setting\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient was treated in the emergency department.\"\nSOURCE: \"treated\" => intervention; TARGET: \"emergency department\" => setting\nRELATION: SOURCE => has setting => TARGET\n\"The wound was managed at home.\"\nSOURCE: \"wound management\" => intervention; TARGET: \"at home\" => setting\nRELATION: SOURCE => has setting => TARGET\n\"He was monitored in the intensive care unit.\"\nSOURCE: \"monitored\" => task; TARGET: \"intensive care unit\" => setting\nRELATION: SOURCE => has setting => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000060
name: intention
def: "Modifies a relation to indicate that the relation is intended rather than actual. Presence-only: the axis has no value set, so the qualifier is either asserted or absent." []
is_a: CLCO:0000067 ! qualifier
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"will start chemotherapy\" => intention\n\"intended to undergo surgery\" => intention\n\"plans to begin therapy\" => intention\n\"scheduled for an MRI\" => intention\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"underwent surgery\" => completed, NOT intention\n\"recommended an MRI\" => recommended, NOT intention\n\"may have pneumonia\" => uncertainty, NOT intention\n\"had pneumonia last year\" => historical, NOT intention\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient will start chemotherapy.\"\nSOURCE: \"chemotherapy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"will start\" => intention\nRELATION: SOURCE => has intention => TARGET\n\"The patient intended to undergo surgery.\"\nSOURCE: \"surgery\" => intervention; TARGET: \"intended\" => intention\nRELATION: SOURCE => has intention => TARGET\n\"She plans to begin physical therapy.\"\nSOURCE: \"physical therapy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"plans to begin\" => intention\nRELATION: SOURCE => has intention => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Epistemic modality axis: captures whether the association describes an actual event or an intended/planned one. Orthogonal to temporal_frame (CLCO_0000082), which captures WHEN relative to the document, and completion_status (CLCO_0000063), which captures workflow state. An intended event may be past (we intended chemo but did not start), present, or future." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000062
name: recommended
def: "The modified relationship is recommended, for example an intervention, admission or some action. Presence-only: the axis has no value set, so the qualifier is either asserted or absent." []
is_a: CLCO:0000067 ! qualifier
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"recommended an MRI\" => recommended\n\"should follow up\" => recommended\n\"advised to stop smoking\" => recommended\n\"the patient was told to rest\" => recommended\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"underwent an MRI\" => completed, NOT recommended\n\"will undergo surgery\" => intention, NOT recommended\n\"may have pneumonia\" => uncertainty, NOT recommended\n\"denied chest pain\" => negation, NOT recommended\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The physician recommended an MRI.\"\nSOURCE: \"MRI\" => intervention; TARGET: \"recommended\" => recommended\nRELATION: SOURCE => has recommended => TARGET\n\"The patient should follow up in two weeks.\"\nSOURCE: \"follow up\" => intervention; TARGET: \"should\" => recommended\nRELATION: SOURCE => has recommended => TARGET\n\"She was advised to stop smoking.\"\nSOURCE: \"stop smoking\" => intervention; TARGET: \"advised\" => recommended\nRELATION: SOURCE => has recommended => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000063
name: completion status
def: "The workflow completion state of a process. Orthogonal to temporal_frame (which captures when relative to the document) and intention (which captures intent). A process may be pending regardless of whether its temporal frame is past, present, or future." []
xref: OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4138595
xref: SNOMED:40642538
is_a: CLCO:0000067 ! qualifier
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"pending\" => completion status\n\"in progress\" => completion status\n\"completed\" => completion status\n\"finished\" => completion status\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"will undergo\" => intention, NOT completion status\n\"recommended\" => recommended, NOT completion status\n\"may undergo\" => uncertainty, NOT completion status\n\"last year\" => historical, NOT completion status\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The CT results are pending.\"\nSOURCE: \"CT results\" => finding; TARGET: \"pending\" => completion status\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\"The biopsy is in progress.\"\nSOURCE: \"biopsy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"in progress\" => completion status\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\"The procedure was completed.\"\nSOURCE: \"procedure\" => intervention; TARGET: \"completed\" => completion status\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Refactored from the original \"status\" class. Children include pending (moved from temporal), in_progress, and completed. Aligns with SNOMED procedure status qualifier values and EHR order status fields. No equivalent in NLP temporal annotation schemes like THYME or I2b2." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000065
name: pending
def: "The process described by the association has been initiated (e.g., ordered, requested) but has not yet reached its terminal output state. This is a workflow status, not a temporal frame: a pending result may refer to a process that occurred in the past (e.g., labs drawn yesterday, results pending)." []
xref: SNOMED:385645004
is_a: CLCO:0000063 ! completion status
disjoint_from: CLCO:0000087 ! in progress
property_value: IAO:0000112 "CT results pending" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"results pending\" => pending\n\"awaiting pathology\" => pending\n\"order pending\" => pending\n\"not yet resulted\" => pending\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"procedure completed\" => completed, NOT pending\n\"currently receiving therapy\" => in progress, NOT pending\n\"will undergo surgery\" => intention, NOT pending\n\"last year\" => historical, NOT pending\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The CT results are pending.\"\nSOURCE: \"CT results\" => finding; TARGET: \"pending\" => pending\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\"The pathology report is still pending.\"\nSOURCE: \"pathology report\" => documentation; TARGET: \"pending\" => pending\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\"The laboratory order remains pending.\"\nSOURCE: \"laboratory order\" => intervention; TARGET: \"pending\" => pending\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Moved from subClassOf temporal (CLCO_0000064) to subClassOf completion_status (CLCO_0000063). The previous definition conflated workflow state with temporal frame and epistemic modality. See temporal_plan.txt Section 1A for rationale." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000067
name: qualifier
def: "A modifier that provides additional context to a clinical association, such as temporal frame, certainty, negation, or participant-level detail." []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"suspected\" => qualifier\n\"denied\" => qualifier\n\"pending\" => qualifier\n\"last year\" => qualifier\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"chest pain\" => finding, NOT qualifier\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT qualifier\n\"physician\" => clinician, NOT qualifier\n\"three weeks\" => time, NOT qualifier\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"A tumor was suspected.\"\nSOURCE: \"tumor\" => finding; TARGET: \"suspected\" => qualifier\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\"The patient denied fever.\"\nSOURCE: \"fever\" => finding; TARGET: \"denied\" => qualifier\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\"The results are pending.\"\nSOURCE: \"results\" => finding; TARGET: \"pending\" => qualifier\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Renamed from \"association qualifier\" on 2026-10-20. The class names the qualifier axis only; what the qualifier scopes over is carried by the property used to attach it (has association qualifier, has subject qualifier, has object qualifier). The former name read as a commitment to statement scope, which the class does not make. Direct children are the six orthogonal axes." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000068
name: obsolete statement qualifier
def: "An association qualifier that modifies the entire clinical statement, such as intention, recommendation or completion status." []
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Obsoleted 2026-10-19. Qualifier scope is carried by the qualifier property, not by the qualifier class: has association qualifier (CLCO:0003000) attaches a qualifier to the whole association, has subject qualifier (CLCO:0003001) and has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002) attach it to a single participant. Encoding scope in the class hierarchy as well could not express the axis/scope cross-product -- negation (CLCO:0000080) and uncertainty (CLCO:0000081) were never subclasses of this class, so statement-scoped negation had no class to begin with. The class hierarchy now holds only the orthogonal qualifier axes. Former children intention (CLCO:0000060), recommended (CLCO:0000062) and completion status (CLCO:0000063) are now direct subclasses of association qualifier (CLCO:0000067); that they are statement-only is now asserted as the range of has participant qualifier instead." xsd:string
is_obsolete: true
consider: CLCO:0003000

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000069
name: obsolete predicate qualifier
def: "An association qualifier that modifies only the predicate (relationship type) of a clinical association, rather than the entire statement." []
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Obsoleted 2026-10-19. Qualifier scope is carried by the qualifier property, not by the qualifier class: has association qualifier (CLCO:0003000) attaches a qualifier to the whole association, has subject qualifier (CLCO:0003001) and has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002) attach it to a single participant. Encoding scope in the class hierarchy as well could not express the axis/scope cross-product -- negation (CLCO:0000080) and uncertainty (CLCO:0000081) were never subclasses of this class, so statement-scoped negation had no class to begin with. The class hierarchy now holds only the orthogonal qualifier axes. No instances were ever modelled and the class had no children. In a reified model the association node is anchored on the predicate itself, so a predicate-scoped qualifier is not distinguishable from a statement-scoped one during annotation. All three of its former contextual examples were in fact uncertainty, historical (CLCO:0000083) and negation, which already carry that guidance. Add a has predicate qualifier sub-property if a genuine predicate-scoped case is ever found." xsd:string
is_obsolete: true
consider: CLCO:0003000

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000071
name: obsolete has aspect
def: "A finding association specifying which facet, part, or functional dimension of an entity is being referred to in the assertion." []
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Obsoleted 2026-10-23. Every pattern this class was created for is expressible with existing vocabulary once the noun phrase is typed as a finding: \"Bone density is decreasing\" is has course (CLCO:0000051) over the finding \"bone density\"; \"Cancer progression is rapid\" is has course over \"cancer progression\", and course (CLCO:0000105) already lists \"Rapidly progressing\" among its own values; \"Cardiac function is preserved\" is has descriptive value (CLCO:0000075) over \"cardiac function\". All three have been moved to those classes. Four further reasons: the class had no cue -- every other association is licensed by a verb, preposition or connective, while aspect was licensed only by noun-noun juxtaposition, leaving no span to annotate; all three of its own contextual examples contradicted its own restrictions, using a finding site subject where finding was declared and a course object where value was declared; it shared the finding-to-value signature with has severity, has value, has descriptive value, has quantifiable value and now has laterality, adding no discriminating power; and its negative examples had to borrow has laterality and has spatial orientation to say what it was not. What aspect reached for -- density or function as a measurable property of a site -- is the SNOMED CT observable entity axis, which CLCO does not model. Should CLCO ever post-coordinate against LOINC, where the property axis is first class, or against SNOMED observable entities, that capability should return as an observable entity class on the clinical entity side, not as a finding-to-value association. Obsoleting this class does not foreclose it." xsd:string
is_obsolete: true
consider: CLCO:0000051, CLCO:0000075, CLCO:0000024

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000072
name: has spatial orientation
def: "A finding association specifying the spatial orientation or anatomical direction of a finding relative to a body site." []
is_a: CLCO:0000057 ! clinical association
relationship: CLCO:0002501 CLCO:0000112 ! has object finding site
relationship: CLCO:0002502 CLCO:0000101 ! has subject finding
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"anterior to the knee\" => has spatial orientation\n\"below the diaphragm\" => has spatial orientation\n\"posterior to the heart\" => has spatial orientation\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"left knee\" => has laterality, NOT has spatial orientation\n\"severe pain\" => has severity, NOT has spatial orientation\n\"three weeks\" => has duration, NOT has spatial orientation\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The lesion is anterior to the knee.\"\nSOURCE: \"lesion\" => finding; TARGET: \"anterior to the knee\" => finding site\nRELATION: SOURCE => has spatial orientation => TARGET\n\"The mass is below the diaphragm.\"\nSOURCE: \"mass\" => finding; TARGET: \"below the diaphragm\" => finding site\nRELATION: SOURCE => has spatial orientation => TARGET\n\"The opacity is posterior to the heart.\"\nSOURCE: \"opacity\" => finding; TARGET: \"posterior to the heart\" => finding site\nRELATION: SOURCE => has spatial orientation => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "The lesion is located on the anterior aspect of the left knee." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Spatial orientation qualifiers reuse PATO quality terms directly; CLCO defines only the attachment role." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000073
name: has laterality
def: "A finding association specifying the laterality (left, right, bilateral, unilateral, or midline) of a finding. The object is the laterality value itself; the body site, where stated, is carried separately by has location." []
is_a: CLCO:0000057 ! clinical association
relationship: CLCO:0002501 CLCO:0000106 ! has object value
relationship: CLCO:0002502 CLCO:0000101 ! has subject finding
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"left\" => has laterality\n\"right-sided\" => has laterality\n\"bilateral\" => has laterality\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"anterior\" => has spatial orientation, NOT has laterality\n\"severe\" => has severity, NOT has laterality\n\"intermittent\" => has course, NOT has laterality\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient has left knee pain.\"\nSOURCE: \"knee pain\" => finding; TARGET: \"left\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has laterality => TARGET\n\"A right-sided pneumothorax was seen.\"\nSOURCE: \"pneumothorax\" => finding; TARGET: \"right-sided\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has laterality => TARGET\n\"She has bilateral knee pain.\"\nSOURCE: \"knee pain\" => finding; TARGET: \"bilateral\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has laterality => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Right-sided pneumothorax; bilateral knee pain." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Object changed from finding site (CLCO:0000112) to value (CLCO:0000106) on 2026-10-21. The previous restriction did not match the class's own examples: \"left\", \"right-sided\" and \"bilateral\" are laterality values, not body sites, whereas the sibling has spatial orientation (CLCO:0000072) genuinely does take a site (\"anterior to the knee\"). Where a site is also stated, express it separately with has location (CLCO:0000023).\n\nRecorded alternative, not adopted: an earlier draft modelled this as a participant-scoped qualifier over PATO quality terms rather than as an association --\n\n  laterality_qualifier\n    ⊑ has_participant_qualifier only\n       (PATO:0000611  # left\n        or PATO:0000612  # right\n        or PATO:0000613  # bilateral\n        or PATO:0000614  # unilateral\n        or PATO:0000610) # midline\n\nThat remains defensible: \"left\" in \"left knee pain\" modifies the knee, which is participant scope, and the draft would now use has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002). It was not adopted because the qualifier family is currently all-modal -- negation, certainty, temporal frame, completion status, intention, recommended -- and admitting a physical quality axis would mean widening the range of the participant properties, which is what encodes the restriction to scope-polymorphic modal axes. Revisit together with has spatial orientation, whose own note states the same PATO intent." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000074
name: has severity
def: "A finding association specifying the severity or intensity of a finding or condition." []
xref: HP:0012824
is_a: CLCO:0000057 ! clinical association
relationship: CLCO:0002501 CLCO:0000106 ! has object value
relationship: CLCO:0002502 CLCO:0000101 ! has subject finding
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"severe\" => has severity\n\"mild\" => has severity\n\"moderate\" => has severity\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"worsening\" => has course, NOT has severity\n\"left\" => has laterality, NOT has severity\n\"for three weeks\" => has duration, NOT has severity\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient has severe abdominal pain.\"\nSOURCE: \"abdominal pain\" => finding; TARGET: \"severe\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has severity => TARGET\n\"She reports mild hearing loss.\"\nSOURCE: \"hearing loss\" => finding; TARGET: \"mild\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has severity => TARGET\n\"He has moderate shortness of breath.\"\nSOURCE: \"shortness of breath\" => finding; TARGET: \"moderate\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has severity => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Severe abdominal pain; mild hearing loss." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000075
name: has descriptive value
def: "Information that qualitatively describes a finding, condition, or intervention." []
is_a: CLCO:0000024 ! has value
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Patient describes dizziness as a room spinning sensation." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"room-spinning\" => has descriptive value\n\"pressure-like\" => has descriptive value\n\"nonproductive\" => has descriptive value\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"38.5 degrees Celsius\" => has quantifiable value, NOT has descriptive value\n\"headache\" => finding, NOT has descriptive value\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT has descriptive value\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient described dizziness as room-spinning.\"\nSOURCE: \"dizziness\" => finding; TARGET: \"room-spinning\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has descriptive value => TARGET\n\"She described the pain as pressure-like.\"\nSOURCE: \"pain\" => finding; TARGET: \"pressure-like\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has descriptive value => TARGET\n\"The cough was nonproductive.\"\nSOURCE: \"cough\" => finding; TARGET: \"nonproductive\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has descriptive value => TARGET\n\"Cardiac function is preserved.\"\nSOURCE: \"cardiac function\" => finding; TARGET: \"preserved\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has descriptive value => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000076
name: has quantifiable value
def: "Information that numerically quantifies a finding, condition, or intervention." []
xref: IAO:0000109
is_a: CLCO:0000024 ! has value
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Blood pressure 130/80 mmHg; hemoglobin 10.2 g/dL." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"38.5 degrees Celsius\" => has quantifiable value\n\"120/80 mmHg\" => has quantifiable value\n\"10.2 g/dL\" => has quantifiable value\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"severe\" => has descriptive value or has severity, NOT has quantifiable value\n\"fever\" => finding, NOT has quantifiable value\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT has quantifiable value\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The temperature was 38.5 degrees Celsius.\"\nSOURCE: \"temperature\" => finding; TARGET: \"38.5 degrees Celsius\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has quantifiable value => TARGET\n\"Blood pressure was 120/80 mmHg.\"\nSOURCE: \"blood pressure\" => finding; TARGET: \"120/80 mmHg\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has quantifiable value => TARGET\n\"Hemoglobin was 10.2 g/dL.\"\nSOURCE: \"hemoglobin\" => finding; TARGET: \"10.2 g/dL\" => value\nRELATION: SOURCE => has quantifiable value => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000077
name: suggests finding
def: "A finding or condition suggested by a diagnostic process, documentation, another finding or condition, or an intervention." []
is_a: CLCO:0000006 ! clinical explanation
relationship: CLCO:0002501 CLCO:0000101 ! has object finding
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"imaging suggested pneumonia\" => suggests finding\n\"the note raised concern for malignancy\" => suggests finding\n\"the symptom pattern pointed to appendicitis\" => suggests finding\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"imaging confirmed pneumonia\" => is consistent with diagnosis, NOT suggests finding\n\"the patient denied pneumonia\" => negation, NOT suggests finding\n\"MRI was ordered for headache\" => has reason, NOT suggests finding\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The chest x-ray suggested pneumonia.\"\nSOURCE: \"chest x-ray\" => intervention; TARGET: \"pneumonia\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => suggests finding => TARGET\n\"The note raised concern for malignancy.\"\nSOURCE: \"note\" => documentation; TARGET: \"malignancy\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => suggests finding => TARGET\n\"The symptom pattern pointed to appendicitis.\"\nSOURCE: \"symptom pattern\" => finding; TARGET: \"appendicitis\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => suggests finding => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "The pink sputum suggests hemoptysis." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000080
name: negation
def: "Signifies that the qualified element is negated. Applies at any scope: statement-level negation negates the entire association; participant-level negation negates a specific subject or object." []
is_a: CLCO:0000067 ! qualifier
property_value: IAO:0000112 "\"Patient denies chest pain\" (statement-level); \"Tenderness is present, but not in the right upper quadrant\" (participant-level)." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"denied\" => negation\n\"no evidence of\" => negation\n\"without\" => negation\n\"not present\" => negation\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"suspected\" => uncertainty, NOT negation\n\"recommended\" => recommended, NOT negation\n\"completed\" => completed, NOT negation\n\"severe\" => value, NOT negation\n\"not always present\" => do not negate the finding without checking scope\n\nNegation cues must be interpreted with their scope. The word \"not\" alone does not always negate the clinical finding.\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient denied having a fever.\"\nSOURCE: \"fever\" => finding; TARGET: \"denied\" => negation\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\"No evidence of pneumonia was found.\"\nSOURCE: \"pneumonia\" => finding; TARGET: \"no evidence\" => negation\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\"There was no fracture.\"\nSOURCE: \"fracture\" => finding; TARGET: \"no\" => negation\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\nPARTICIPANT-SCOPED EXAMPLE:\n\"Tenderness is present, but not in the right upper quadrant.\"\nSOURCE: \"tenderness\" => finding; TARGET: \"not\" => negation\nRELATION: SOURCE => has object qualifier => TARGET\nThe finding is asserted and only its site is negated, so the negation attaches to the participant\nfilling the object slot. Using has association qualifier here would wrongly deny the tenderness.\nNegation and uncertainty are the only two axes that may be attached at participant scope." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000081
name: uncertainty
def: "Signifies that the qualified element is uncertain or suspected. Applies at any scope: statement-level uncertainty qualifies the entire association; participant-level uncertainty qualifies a specific subject or object." []
is_a: CLCO:0000067 ! qualifier
property_value: IAO:0000112 "\"The patient was possibly treated with antibiotics elsewhere\" (statement-level: the treatment is what is uncertain); \"Possible pneumonia was treated with antibiotics\" (participant-level: the treatment happened, the diagnosis is uncertain)." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"suspected\" => uncertainty\n\"possible\" => uncertainty\n\"probable\" => uncertainty\n\"may have\" => uncertainty\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"denied\" => negation, NOT uncertainty\n\"recommended\" => recommended, NOT uncertainty\n\"completed\" => completed, NOT uncertainty\n\"severe\" => value, NOT uncertainty\n\"does not exclude\" => uncertainty, NOT negation\n\n\"Does not exclude pulmonary embolism\" indicates that pulmonary embolism remains possible; it does not assert that pulmonary embolism is absent.\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"A soft-tissue tumor was suspected.\"\nSOURCE: \"soft-tissue tumor\" => finding; TARGET: \"suspected\" => uncertainty\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\"CT findings suggested possible pneumonia.\"\nSOURCE: \"pneumonia\" => finding; TARGET: \"possible\" => uncertainty\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\"The patient may have a pulmonary embolism.\"\nSOURCE: \"pulmonary embolism\" => finding; TARGET: \"may have\" => uncertainty\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\nPARTICIPANT-SCOPED EXAMPLE:\n\"Possible pneumonia was treated with antibiotics.\"\nSOURCE: \"pneumonia\" => finding; TARGET: \"Possible\" => uncertainty\nRELATION: SOURCE => has subject qualifier => TARGET\nThe treatment did happen and only the diagnosis is uncertain, so the uncertainty attaches to the\nparticipant filling the subject slot. Using has association qualifier here would wrongly say the\ntreatment may not have happened. Negation and uncertainty are the only two axes that may be\nattached at participant scope." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000082
name: temporal frame
def: "The temporal location of the association relative to the moment of clinical documentation. Orthogonal to completion_status and intention." []
xref: biolink:temporal_context_qualifier
is_a: CLCO:0000067 ! qualifier
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"last year\" => temporal frame\n\"currently\" => temporal frame\n\"tomorrow\" => temporal frame\n\"if symptoms recur\" => temporal frame\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"three weeks\" => time, NOT temporal frame\n\"will start\" => intention, NOT temporal frame\n\"pending\" => completion status, NOT temporal frame\n\"suspected\" => uncertainty, NOT temporal frame\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient had pneumonia last year.\"\nSOURCE: \"pneumonia\" => finding; TARGET: \"last year\" => temporal frame\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"The patient will undergo surgery tomorrow.\"\nSOURCE: \"surgery\" => intervention; TARGET: \"tomorrow\" => temporal frame\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"If symptoms recur, restart treatment.\"\nSOURCE: \"restart treatment\" => intervention; TARGET: \"if symptoms recur\" => temporal frame\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Currently statement-scoped only: this class is excluded from the range of has subject qualifier (CLCO:0003001) and has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002), unlike negation (CLCO:0000080) and uncertainty (CLCO:0000081), whose definitions state that they apply at any scope. This may be restructured as participant-scopeable depending on future time series work that will better integrate TimeML and DocTimeRel. The motivating pattern is a participant whose temporal frame differs from the association, for example \"history of MI, now on aspirin\", where the subject is historical but the association is current." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Replaces the deprecated temporal (CLCO_0000064). Aligns with THYME DocTimeRel and MedSpaCy temporal context flags. This axis answers WHEN relative to the document, not whether a process is complete (completion_status) or committed (intention)." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000083
name: historical
def: "The association describes an event or state that occurred before the time of the clinical document." []
xref: THYME:DocTimeRel_BEFORE
is_a: CLCO:0000082 ! temporal frame
disjoint_from: CLCO:0000084 ! current
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Patient underwent two kidney transplants (2002, 2012)" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"last year\" => historical\n\"previously\" => historical\n\"history of\" => historical\n\"in childhood\" => historical\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"currently\" => current, NOT historical\n\"tomorrow\" => future, NOT historical\n\"may occur\" => hypothetical, NOT historical\n\"pending\" => pending, NOT historical\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient had pneumonia last year.\"\nSOURCE: \"pneumonia\" => finding; TARGET: \"last year\" => historical\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"She previously underwent surgery.\"\nSOURCE: \"surgery\" => intervention; TARGET: \"previously\" => historical\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"He has a history of diabetes.\"\nSOURCE: \"diabetes\" => finding; TARGET: \"history of\" => historical\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000084
name: current
def: "The association describes an event or state that overlaps with the time of the clinical document." []
xref: THYME:DocTimeRel_OVERLAP
is_a: CLCO:0000082 ! temporal frame
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Currently on metformin" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"currently\" => current\n\"now\" => current\n\"at present\" => current\n\"today\" => current\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"last year\" => historical, NOT current\n\"tomorrow\" => future, NOT current\n\"if symptoms recur\" => hypothetical, NOT current\n\"pending\" => pending, NOT current\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient is currently on metformin.\"\nSOURCE: \"on metformin\" => intervention; TARGET: \"currently\" => current\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"The infection is present now.\"\nSOURCE: \"infection\" => finding; TARGET: \"now\" => current\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"The patient is currently receiving therapy.\"\nSOURCE: \"receiving therapy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"currently\" => current\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000085
name: future
def: "The association describes an event or state that is expected to occur after the time of the clinical document." []
xref: THYME:DocTimeRel_AFTER
is_a: CLCO:0000082 ! temporal frame
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Chemotherapy will begin next Tuesday" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"tomorrow\" => future\n\"next week\" => future\n\"will begin\" => future\n\"scheduled for next month\" => future\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"last year\" => historical, NOT future\n\"currently\" => current, NOT future\n\"if symptoms recur\" => hypothetical, NOT future\n\"pending\" => pending, NOT future\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"Chemotherapy will begin next Tuesday.\"\nSOURCE: \"chemotherapy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"next Tuesday\" => future\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"The patient will undergo surgery tomorrow.\"\nSOURCE: \"surgery\" => intervention; TARGET: \"tomorrow\" => future\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"A follow-up visit is scheduled for next month.\"\nSOURCE: \"follow-up visit\" => intervention; TARGET: \"next month\" => future\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000086
name: hypothetical
def: "The association describes a conditional or contingent event that may or may not occur depending on specified circumstances." []
xref: THYME:contextual_modality_HYPOTHETICAL
is_a: CLCO:0000082 ! temporal frame
property_value: IAO:0000112 "If fever persists, start vancomycin" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"if symptoms recur\" => hypothetical\n\"should fever develop\" => hypothetical\n\"in case of bleeding\" => hypothetical\n\"could require admission\" => hypothetical\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"last year\" => historical, NOT hypothetical\n\"currently\" => current, NOT hypothetical\n\"tomorrow\" => future, NOT hypothetical\n\"completed\" => completed, NOT hypothetical\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"If symptoms recur, restart treatment.\"\nSOURCE: \"restart treatment\" => intervention; TARGET: \"if symptoms recur\" => hypothetical\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"Should fever develop, call the clinic.\"\nSOURCE: \"call the clinic\" => task; TARGET: \"Should fever develop\" => hypothetical\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\"The patient could require admission.\"\nSOURCE: \"admission\" => intervention; TARGET: \"could require\" => hypothetical\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Sits at the boundary of temporal frame and modality. Placed under temporal_frame because NLP systems (THYME contextual_modality, MedSpaCy is_hypothetical) treat it as a document-context label at the same annotation layer as historical/current/future." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000087
name: in progress
def: "The process described by the association is actively executing but has not yet reached its terminal state." []
is_a: CLCO:0000063 ! completion status
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Antibiotics course ongoing" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"in progress\" => in progress\n\"ongoing\" => in progress\n\"currently receiving\" => in progress\n\"underway\" => in progress\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"pending\" => pending, NOT in progress\n\"completed\" => completed, NOT in progress\n\"will begin\" => future or intention, NOT in progress\n\"last year\" => historical, NOT in progress\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The antibiotic course is in progress.\"\nSOURCE: \"antibiotic course\" => intervention; TARGET: \"in progress\" => in progress\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\"Physical therapy is ongoing.\"\nSOURCE: \"physical therapy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"ongoing\" => in progress\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\"The patient is currently receiving chemotherapy.\"\nSOURCE: \"chemotherapy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"currently receiving\" => in progress\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000088
name: completed
def: "The process described by the association has reached its terminal output state." []
is_a: CLCO:0000063 ! completion status
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Physical therapy completed" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"completed\" => completed\n\"finished\" => completed\n\"performed\" => completed\n\"concluded\" => completed\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"pending\" => pending, NOT completed\n\"in progress\" => in progress, NOT completed\n\"will undergo\" => intention or future, NOT completed\n\"may undergo\" => uncertainty, NOT completed\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The biopsy was completed.\"\nSOURCE: \"biopsy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"completed\" => completed\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\"The procedure was performed.\"\nSOURCE: \"procedure\" => intervention; TARGET: \"performed\" => completed\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\"Physical therapy has concluded.\"\nSOURCE: \"physical therapy\" => intervention; TARGET: \"concluded\" => completed\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000100
name: clinical entity
def: "A core clinical entity over which all clinical context associations occur." []
is_a: BFO:0000001 ! entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES: patient, chest pain, and appendectomy are clinical entities.\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES: has, severely, and because are a relation, modifier, and conjunction rather than clinical entities.\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: In \"The patient has chest pain\", patient and chest pain are clinical entities; in \"Appendectomy was scheduled\", appendectomy is a clinical entity." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "The 14 core clinical entity classes defined in:\nColicchio, Tiago K., Pavithra I. Dissanayake, and James J. Cimino. \"Formal representation of patients’ care context data: the path to improving the electronic health record.\" Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association 27, no. 11 (2020): 1648-1657.\nAll of these should correspond to a subject or object in relations extracted by NLP systems. The exception to that is patient which may be inferred." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000101
name: finding
def: "A clinical finding of any type, including conditions, diagnosis and assessments." []
xref: biolink:DiseaseOrPhenotypicFeature
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Chest pain\" => finding\n\"Fever\" => finding\n\"Headache\" => finding\n\"Muscle weakness\" => finding\n\"Shortness of breath\" => finding\n\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT finding\n\"Biopsy\" => intervention, NOT finding\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT finding\n\"Mother\" => family member, NOT finding\n\"Three weeks\" => time, NOT finding\n\"Worsening\" => course, NOT finding\n\"Severe\" => value, NOT finding\n\"Suspected\" => uncertainty, NOT finding\n\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient presented with severe chest pain.\"\nAnnotate: \"chest pain\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"severe\" => value\n\n\"The patient reported progressively worsening muscle weakness.\"\nAnnotate: \"muscle weakness\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"progressively worsening\" => course\n\n\"MRI revealed a pulmonary nodule.\"\nAnnotate: \"pulmonary nodule\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"MRI\" => intervention\n\n\"The patient experienced intermittent headaches for three weeks.\"\nAnnotate: \"headaches\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"intermittent\" => course\nAnnotate: \"three weeks\" => time" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Was finding/condition in original paper, can treat condition as a subclass if needed." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000102
name: intervention
def: "An intervention to treat or diagnose a finding/condition or the patient" []
xref: biolink:Procedure
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"MRI\" => intervention\n\"Biopsy\" => intervention\n\"Surgery\" => intervention\n\"Antibiotic treatment\" => intervention\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT intervention\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT intervention\n\"Three weeks\" => time, NOT intervention\n\"Hospital\" => setting, NOT intervention\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient underwent an MRI.\"\nAnnotate: \"MRI\" => intervention\n\n\"A biopsy was performed to evaluate the mass.\"\nAnnotate: \"biopsy\" => intervention\nAnnotate: \"mass\" => finding\n\n\"The patient started antibiotic treatment for pneumonia.\"\nAnnotate: \"antibiotic treatment\" => intervention\nAnnotate: \"pneumonia\" => finding" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "There is not a SNOMED code for this as of 08/19/2026 documented in the athena ohdsi database." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000103
name: time
def: "Numerical or narrative temporal data elements" []
xref: SNOMEDCT:410669006
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Three weeks\" => time\n\"Yesterday\" => time\n\"Since childhood\" => time\n\"For two months\" => time\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT time\n\"Worsening\" => course, NOT time\n\"Severe\" => value, NOT time\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT time\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient has had headaches for three weeks.\"\nAnnotate: \"headaches\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"three weeks\" => time\n\n\"The symptoms began yesterday.\"\nAnnotate: \"symptoms\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"yesterday\" => time\n\n\"The patient has experienced pain since childhood.\"\nAnnotate: \"pain\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"since childhood\" => time" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Moved from subClassOf task (CLCO_0000109) to subClassOf clinical_entity (CLCO_0000100). Time is a first-class clinical entity type, not a subtype of task." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000104
name: reason
def: "Justifications and reasons for ordering, performing, planning, or discontinuing an intervention or diagnostic process" []
xref: SNOMEDCT:288830005
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Because of worsening pain\" => reason\n\"History of diabetes\" => reason\n\"Abnormal imaging result\" => reason\n\"Patient preference\" => reason\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT reason\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT reason\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT reason\n\"Three weeks\" => time, NOT reason\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The MRI was ordered because of persistent headaches.\"\nAnnotate: \"MRI\" => intervention\nAnnotate: \"persistent headaches\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"because of persistent headaches\" => reason\n\n\"Surgery was postponed due to the patient's cardiac risk.\"\nAnnotate: \"surgery\" => intervention\nAnnotate: \"cardiac risk\" => reason" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "SNOMEDCT sourced from Athena OHDSI \"Reason and justification\" (https://athena.ohdsi.org/search-terms/terms/4128496)" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000105
name: course
def: "Course of a finding/condition" []
xref: SNOMEDCT:260908002
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Stable\" => course\n\"Worsening\" => course\n\"Intermittent\" => course\n\"Rapidly progressing\" => course\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Two weeks\" => time, not course\n\"sudden onset\" => time, not course\n\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient reported progressively worsening weakness.\"\nAnnotate: \"progressively worsening\" => course\nAnnotate: \"weakness\" => finding\n\n\"The patient's symptoms have remained stable.\"\nAnnotate: \"stable\" => course\n\n\"The patient experienced intermittent episodes of chest pain.\"\nAnnotate: \"intermittent\" => course" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000106
name: value
def: "Any numerical or narrative description of a finding/condition or intervention" []
xref: SNOWMEDCT:83568003
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"38.5 degrees Celsius\" => value\n\"120/80 mmHg\" => value\n\"Positive\" => value\n\"No improvement\" => value\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Fever\" => finding, NOT value\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT value\n\"Three weeks\" => time, NOT value\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient's temperature was 38.5 degrees Celsius.\"\nAnnotate: \"temperature\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"38.5 degrees Celsius\" => value\n\n\"The CT result was positive for pneumonia.\"\nAnnotate: \"CT\" => intervention\nAnnotate: \"positive\" => value\nAnnotate: \"pneumonia\" => finding" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "SNOWMEDCT code for \"hasvalue\" sourced from Athena OHDSI database (https://athena.ohdsi.org/search-terms/terms/4306768)" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000107
name: setting
def: "Health care setting or location" []
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Emergency department\" => setting\n\"Intensive care unit\" => setting\n\"Outpatient clinic\" => setting\n\"Home\" => setting\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT setting\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT setting\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT setting\n\"Three weeks\" => time, NOT setting\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient was admitted to the intensive care unit.\"\nAnnotate: \"patient\" => patient\nAnnotate: \"intensive care unit\" => setting\n\n\"The procedure was performed in the outpatient clinic.\"\nAnnotate: \"procedure\" => intervention\nAnnotate: \"outpatient clinic\" => setting" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "There is not a SNOMED code for this as of 08/19/2026 documented in the athena ohdsi database." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000108
name: clinician
def: "Health care professional, unlike SNOMED, includes only people working directly with patients such as physicians, nurses, etc... Administrative healthcare professionals such as healthcare billing coders are not included." []
xref: SNOMEDCT:44804106
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Physician\" => clinician\n\"Nurse practitioner\" => clinician\n\"Physician assistant\" => clinician\n\"Radiologist\" => clinician\n\"Pathologist\" => clinician\n\"Pharmacist\" => clinician\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Mother\" => family member, NOT clinician\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT clinician\n\"30-year-old male patient\" => patient, NOT clinician" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000109
name: task
def: "Any healthcare related task not related to direct clinical activities (e.g., phone call or uploading a medical record file)." []
xref: SNOMEDCT:101878003
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Phone call\" => task\n\"Uploading a medical record\" => task\n\"Scheduling an appointment\" => task\n\"Reviewing the chart\" => task\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT task\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT task\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT task\n\"Emergency department\" => setting, NOT task\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The nurse called the patient to confirm the appointment.\"\nAnnotate: \"nurse\" => clinician\nAnnotate: \"called the patient\" => task\n\n\"The staff uploaded the medical record to the portal.\"\nAnnotate: \"uploaded the medical record\" => task\nAnnotate: \"medical record\" => documentation" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "SNOMEDCT code sourced from Athena OHDSI \"TASK\" (https://athena.ohdsi.org/search-terms/terms/4008963)" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000110
name: patient
def: "The patient entity" []
xref: biolink:Case
xref: SNOMEDCT:116154003
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient\" => patient\n\"The 30-year-old man\" => patient\n\"The child\" => patient\n\"She\" => patient, when the clinical note clearly identifies the referent as the patient\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT patient\n\"Mother\" => family member, NOT patient\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT patient\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT patient\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient reported chest pain.\"\nAnnotate: \"patient\" => patient\nAnnotate: \"chest pain\" => finding\n\n\"She underwent surgery for a fractured femur.\"\nAnnotate: \"She\" => patient\nAnnotate: \"surgery\" => intervention\nAnnotate: \"fractured femur\" => finding" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000111
name: documentation
def: "Clinical documentation, e.g., progress notes, imaging reports" []
xref: IAO:0000310
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Medical Record\" => documentation\n\"Discharge summary\" => documentation\n\"Patient chart\" => documentation\n\"Clinical note\" => documentation\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT documentation\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT documentation\n\"Three weeks\" => time, NOT documentation\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT documentation\n\"Worsening\" => course, NOT documentation\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The medical record noted a history of hypertension.\"\nAnnotate: \"medical record\" => documentation\nAnnotate: \"hypertension\" => finding\n\n\"According to the clinical notes, the patient underwent surgery.\"\nAnnotate: According to the \"clinical notes\" => documentation\nAnnotate: \"surgery\" => intervention" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000112
name: finding site
def: "Anatomical site of a finding/condition" []
xref: SNOMED:123037004
xref: UBERON:0001062
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Chest\" => finding site\n\"Cervical spine\" => finding site\n\"Pituitary\" => finding site\n\"Ovary\" => finding site\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT finding site as a whole\n\"Headache\" => finding, NOT finding site\n\"Swelling\" => finding, NOT finding site\n\"MRI\" => intervention, NOT finding site\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The patient reported pain in the left knee.\"\nAnnotate: \"pain\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"left knee\" => finding site\n\n\"The patient presented with swelling of the right ankle.\"\nAnnotate: \"swelling\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"right ankle\" => finding site\n\n\"CT revealed a mass in the left lung.\"\nAnnotate: \"mass\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"left lung\" => finding site\nAnnotate: \"CT\" => intervention\n\n\"The patient experienced tenderness over the lower abdomen.\"\nAnnotate: \"tenderness\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"lower abdomen\" => finding site\n\n\"The patient had a fracture of the left femur.\"\nAnnotate: \"fracture\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"left femur\" => finding site\n\n\"MRI demonstrated a lesion in the right temporal lobe.\"\nAnnotate: \"lesion\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"right temporal lobe\" => finding site\nAnnotate: \"MRI\" => intervention" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000113
name: patient state
def: "Patient state, e.g., stable, improving. The overall patient state, not whether a particular disease or condition is stable or improving." []
xref: SNOWMEDCT:246097001
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Stable\" => patient state\n\"Improving\" => patient state\n\"Unstable\" => patient state\n\"Alert and oriented\" => patient state\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Stable disease\" => course, NOT patient state\n\"Chest pain\" => finding, NOT patient state\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT patient state\n\"Three weeks\" => time, NOT patient state\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient is clinically stable.\"\nAnnotate: \"patient\" => patient\nAnnotate: \"clinically stable\" => patient state\n\n\"The patient is improving after treatment.\"\nAnnotate: \"patient\" => patient\nAnnotate: \"improving\" => patient state\nAnnotate: \"treatment\" => intervention\n\n\"The patient's symptoms are stable.\"\nAnnotate: \"symptoms\" => finding\nAnnotate: \"stable\" => course" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "SNOMEDCT was sourced from Athena OHDSI \"Patient Status\" (http://athena.ohdsi.org/search-terms/terms/4077556)" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000114
name: is discharged
def: "Statement indicating that the patient has been discharged from a clinical setting" []
xref: OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4137031
xref: SNOMED:58000006
is_a: CLCO:0000058 ! has setting
relationship: CLCO:0002502 CLCO:0000110 ! has subject patient
property_value: IAO:0000112 "Patient discharged this morning with family" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"discharged home\" => is discharged\n\"discharged from the hospital\" => is discharged\n\"ready for discharge\" => is discharged\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"admitted to the hospital\" => is admitted, NOT is discharged\n\"transferred to rehabilitation\" => is transferred to, NOT is discharged\n\"referred to cardiology\" => is referred by, NOT is discharged\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient was discharged home.\"\nSOURCE: \"patient\" => patient; TARGET: \"home\" => setting\nRELATION: SOURCE => is discharged => TARGET\n\"She was discharged from the hospital.\"\nSOURCE: \"patient\" => patient; TARGET: \"hospital\" => setting\nRELATION: SOURCE => is discharged => TARGET\n\"He is ready for discharge to a skilled nursing facility.\"\nSOURCE: \"patient\" => patient; TARGET: \"skilled nursing facility\" => setting\nRELATION: SOURCE => is discharged => TARGET" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000115
name: family member
def: "A person who is a member of the patient's family. A caregiver who is not a family member would be identified as a clinician." []
xref: SNOMED:303071001
is_a: CLCO:0000100 ! clinical entity
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Mother\" => family member\n\"Father\" => family member\n\"Sister\" => family member\n\"Brother\" => family member\n\"Daughter\" => family member\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"Patient\" => patient, NOT family member\n\"Physician\" => clinician, NOT family member\n\"Nurse practitioner\" => clinician, NOT family member\n\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The patient's mother has a history of breast cancer.\"\nAnnotate: \"mother\" => family member\nAnnotate: \"breast cancer\" => finding\n\n\"His father was diagnosed with diabetes.\"\nAnnotate: \"father\" => family member\nAnnotate: \"diabetes\" => finding\n\n\"The patient's sister reported similar symptoms.\"\nAnnotate: \"sister\" => family member" xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000116
name: temporal relation
def: "A clinical association asserting the temporal ordering of one finding or intervention relative to another, as stated in the text. Children correspond to the TimeML TLINK relation types that hold between events." []
is_a: CLCO:0000057 ! clinical association
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. Annotation layer for event-to-event temporal ordering. Each child names a text-cued relation an annotator can mark and carries an rdfs:seeAlso to the OWL-Time property that gives its interval semantics. The two layers are deliberately separate: the children here are the cue-bearing subset, while the complete thirteen-relation algebra is derived over time:ProperInterval endpoints, which CLCO already supplies through has start time (CLCO:0002700) and has end time (CLCO:0002701). time:intervalOverlaps and time:intervalOverlappedBy have no child here because TimeML has no relType for partial overlap -- annotators cannot reliably distinguish it from containment in text -- so those two are derivable but never annotated. Event-to-timex links are unchanged and remain has onset, has date, has duration and has frequency. Document-relative time is a separate axis, carried by temporal frame (CLCO:0000082)." xsd:string

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000117
name: follows
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention occurs after another finding or intervention, with a gap permitted between them." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"followed\" => follows\n\"occurred after\" => follows\n\"subsequent to\" => follows\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"preceded\" => precedes, NOT follows\n\"at the same time as\" => is simultaneous with, NOT follows\n\"throughout\" => is included in, NOT follows\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The rash followed the fever.\"\nSOURCE: \"rash\" => finding; TARGET: \"fever\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => follows => TARGET\n\"Delirium developed after the surgery.\"\nSOURCE: \"delirium\" => finding; TARGET: \"surgery\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => follows => TARGET\n\"Dialysis began after the graft failed.\"\nSOURCE: \"dialysis\" => intervention; TARGET: \"graft failure\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => follows => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType AFTER; interval semantics are time:intervalAfter, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalAfter

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000118
name: immediately precedes
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention ends exactly where another begins, with no gap between them." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"immediately before\" => immediately precedes\n\"right before\" => immediately precedes\n\"ended just as\" => immediately precedes\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"before\" => precedes, NOT immediately precedes\n\"at the same time as\" => is simultaneous with, NOT immediately precedes\n\"during\" => is included in, NOT immediately precedes\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The seizure stopped and the post-ictal state began immediately.\"\nSOURCE: \"seizure\" => finding; TARGET: \"post-ictal state\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => immediately precedes => TARGET\n\"Sedation ended and extubation began straight away.\"\nSOURCE: \"sedation\" => intervention; TARGET: \"extubation\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => immediately precedes => TARGET\n\"The infusion finished just as the reaction started.\"\nSOURCE: \"infusion\" => intervention; TARGET: \"reaction\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => immediately precedes => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType IBEFORE; interval semantics are time:intervalMeets, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalMeets

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000119
name: immediately follows
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention begins exactly where another ends, with no gap between them." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"immediately after\" => immediately follows\n\"straight after\" => immediately follows\n\"began as soon as\" => immediately follows\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"after\" => follows, NOT immediately follows\n\"at the same time as\" => is simultaneous with, NOT immediately follows\n\"within\" => is included in, NOT immediately follows\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"Extubation immediately followed the procedure.\"\nSOURCE: \"extubation\" => intervention; TARGET: \"procedure\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => immediately follows => TARGET\n\"The post-ictal state began as soon as the seizure stopped.\"\nSOURCE: \"post-ictal state\" => finding; TARGET: \"seizure\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => immediately follows => TARGET\n\"Hypotension began the moment the infusion stopped.\"\nSOURCE: \"hypotension\" => finding; TARGET: \"infusion\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => immediately follows => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType IAFTER; interval semantics are time:intervalMetBy, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalMetBy

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000120
name: begins
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention starts at the same time as another and ends before it." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"started with\" => begins\n\"opened\" => begins\n\"at the start of\" => begins\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"throughout\" => is simultaneous with, NOT begins\n\"finished with\" => ends, NOT begins\n\"after\" => follows, NOT begins\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The loading dose was given at the start of the antibiotic course.\"\nSOURCE: \"loading dose\" => intervention; TARGET: \"antibiotic course\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => begins => TARGET\n\"Induction opened the anaesthetic.\"\nSOURCE: \"induction\" => intervention; TARGET: \"anaesthetic\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => begins => TARGET\n\"The initial rigor marked the onset of the febrile illness.\"\nSOURCE: \"rigor\" => finding; TARGET: \"febrile illness\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => begins => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType BEGINS; interval semantics are time:intervalStarts, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalStarts

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000121
name: begun by
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention starts at the same time as another and ends after it." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"opened with\" => begun by\n\"started with\" => begun by\n\"began with\" => begun by\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"closed with\" => ended by, NOT begun by\n\"throughout\" => is simultaneous with, NOT begun by\n\"contained\" => includes, NOT begun by\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The antibiotic course opened with a loading dose.\"\nSOURCE: \"antibiotic course\" => intervention; TARGET: \"loading dose\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => begun by => TARGET\n\"The anaesthetic began with induction.\"\nSOURCE: \"anaesthetic\" => intervention; TARGET: \"induction\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => begun by => TARGET\n\"The febrile illness began with a rigor.\"\nSOURCE: \"febrile illness\" => finding; TARGET: \"rigor\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => begun by => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType BEGUN_BY; interval semantics are time:intervalStartedBy, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalStartedBy

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000122
name: ends
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention finishes at the same time as another, having started after it." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"ran to the end of\" => ends\n\"finished with\" => ends\n\"concluded\" => ends\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"started with\" => begins, NOT ends\n\"throughout\" => is simultaneous with, NOT ends\n\"before\" => precedes, NOT ends\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The weaning trial ran to the end of the ventilation episode.\"\nSOURCE: \"weaning trial\" => intervention; TARGET: \"ventilation episode\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => ends => TARGET\n\"The taper concluded the steroid course.\"\nSOURCE: \"taper\" => intervention; TARGET: \"steroid course\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => ends => TARGET\n\"The desaturation persisted to the end of the procedure.\"\nSOURCE: \"desaturation\" => finding; TARGET: \"procedure\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => ends => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType ENDS; interval semantics are time:intervalFinishes, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalFinishes

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000123
name: ended by
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention finishes at the same time as another, having started before it." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"closed with\" => ended by\n\"ended with\" => ended by\n\"concluded with\" => ended by\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"opened with\" => begun by, NOT ended by\n\"throughout\" => is simultaneous with, NOT ended by\n\"spanned\" => includes, NOT ended by\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The ventilation episode closed with a weaning trial.\"\nSOURCE: \"ventilation episode\" => intervention; TARGET: \"weaning trial\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => ended by => TARGET\n\"The steroid course ended with a taper.\"\nSOURCE: \"steroid course\" => intervention; TARGET: \"taper\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => ended by => TARGET\n\"The admission concluded with a discharge review.\"\nSOURCE: \"admission\" => intervention; TARGET: \"discharge review\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => ended by => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType ENDED_BY; interval semantics are time:intervalFinishedBy, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalFinishedBy

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000124
name: is included in
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention falls wholly within the extent of another, sharing neither its beginning nor its end." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"during\" => is included in\n\"while\" => is included in\n\"in the course of\" => is included in\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"spanned\" => includes, NOT is included in\n\"after\" => follows, NOT is included in\n\"started with\" => begins, NOT is included in\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The fever occurred during the admission.\"\nSOURCE: \"fever\" => finding; TARGET: \"admission\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => is included in => TARGET\n\"Atrial fibrillation developed in the course of the sepsis.\"\nSOURCE: \"atrial fibrillation\" => finding; TARGET: \"sepsis\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => is included in => TARGET\n\"A transfusion was given while the patient was in theatre.\"\nSOURCE: \"transfusion\" => intervention; TARGET: \"operation\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => is included in => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType IS_INCLUDED; interval semantics are time:intervalDuring, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalDuring

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000125
name: includes
def: "Statement indicating that a finding or intervention wholly contains the extent of another, sharing neither its beginning nor its end." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"spanned\" => includes\n\"throughout which\" => includes\n\"encompassed\" => includes\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"during\" => is included in, NOT includes\n\"before\" => precedes, NOT includes\n\"closed with\" => ended by, NOT includes\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The admission spanned the episode of delirium.\"\nSOURCE: \"admission\" => intervention; TARGET: \"delirium\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => includes => TARGET\n\"The sepsis encompassed the period of atrial fibrillation.\"\nSOURCE: \"sepsis\" => finding; TARGET: \"atrial fibrillation\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => includes => TARGET\n\"The operation covered the transfusion.\"\nSOURCE: \"operation\" => intervention; TARGET: \"transfusion\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => includes => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType INCLUDES; interval semantics are time:intervalContains, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalContains

[Term]
id: CLCO:0000126
name: is simultaneous with
def: "Statement indicating that two findings or interventions occupy the same extent in time." []
is_a: CLCO:0000116 ! temporal relation
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"at the same time as\" => is simultaneous with\n\"together with\" => is simultaneous with\n\"concurrently\" => is simultaneous with\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\"during\" => is included in, NOT is simultaneous with\n\"after\" => follows, NOT is simultaneous with\n\"started with\" => begins, NOT is simultaneous with\n\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:\n\"The rash and the fever appeared together.\"\nSOURCE: \"rash\" => finding; TARGET: \"fever\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => is simultaneous with => TARGET\n\"The chest pain and the dyspnoea began concurrently.\"\nSOURCE: \"chest pain\" => finding; TARGET: \"dyspnoea\" => finding\nRELATION: SOURCE => is simultaneous with => TARGET\n\"Fluids ran at the same time as the antibiotics.\"\nSOURCE: \"fluid resuscitation\" => intervention; TARGET: \"antibiotics\" => intervention\nRELATION: SOURCE => is simultaneous with => TARGET" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-30. TimeML TLINK relType SIMULTANEOUS; interval semantics are time:intervalEquals, linked by rdfs:seeAlso. Annotated from a text cue between two events; the corresponding interval relation is derived from endpoints rather than annotated." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso intervalEquals

[Term]
id: IAO:0000030
name: information content entity
def: "A generically dependent continuant that is about some entity." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES: a clinical statement, MRI report, and discharge summary are information content entities.\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES: patient, pneumonia, and an MRI machine are respectively a clinical entity, finding, and physical object.\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: In \"The report states that the patient has pneumonia\", the report is an information content entity; MRI report and discharge summary function similarly." xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002000
name: has qualifier
def: "A modifier of a clinical association. Scope-neutral grouping property: annotation should assert through the sub-property that commits to a scope, and this property is used for querying across scopes or for data from a source that did not record scope." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\nUse this property only when the scope of the qualifier is genuinely unknown or deliberately left\nopen, for example in pre-adjudication annotation or when importing data that did not record scope.\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"A soft-tissue tumor was suspected.\"\nUse: has association qualifier, NOT the grouping property has qualifier. The uncertainty applies to\nthe whole statement.\n\n\"Possible pneumonia was treated with antibiotics.\"\nUse: has subject qualifier, NOT the grouping property has qualifier. The treatment happened; only\nthe diagnosis is uncertain.\n\n\"The patient reported pain in his left knee.\"\nUse: has object qualifier, NOT the grouping property has qualifier.\n\nEvery sub-property entails this one, so a query on has qualifier retrieves qualifiers at any scope.\nAnnotation should always commit to a scope." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Analogous to RO:0000053 (has characteristic) in that the association bears the qualifier, but not declared as a sub-property because BFO type constraints require the bearer to be an independent continuant and the characteristic to be a specifically dependent continuant. CLCO associations are information content entities and qualifiers are not modeled as BFO dependent continuants." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Renamed from \"has association qualifier\" on 2026-10-20, when qualifier scope was moved onto the property. This is now the scope-neutral parent; its former label was transferred to CLCO:0003000, which is the statement-scoped child." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso RO:0000053
domain: CLCO:0000057 ! clinical association
range: CLCO:0000067 ! qualifier

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002002
name: has intention
def: "Relates a clinical association to its intention qualifier, indicating that the association is intended rather than actual." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The patient will start chemotherapy.\"\nSOURCE: \"chemotherapy\" => intervention\nTARGET: \"will start\" => intention\nRELATION: SOURCE => has intention => TARGET\n\n\"The patient intended to undergo surgery.\"\nSOURCE: \"surgery\" => intervention\nTARGET: \"intended\" => intention\nRELATION: SOURCE => has intention => TARGET\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLE:\n\n\"The patient underwent surgery.\"\n\"underwent\" describes an actual event, NOT intention." xsd:string
range: CLCO:0000060 ! intention
is_a: CLCO:0003000 ! has association qualifier

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002003
name: has recommended
def: "Relates a clinical association to its recommendation qualifier, indicating that the association represents a clinical recommendation." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The physician recommended an MRI.\"\nSOURCE: \"MRI\" => intervention\nTARGET: \"recommended\" => recommended\nRELATION: SOURCE => has recommended => TARGET\n\n\"The patient should follow up in two weeks.\"\nSOURCE: \"follow up\" => intervention\nTARGET: \"should\" => recommended\nRELATION: SOURCE => has recommended => TARGET\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLE:\n\n\"The patient underwent an MRI.\"\n\"underwent\" describes an actual intervention, NOT a recommendation." xsd:string
range: CLCO:0000062 ! recommended
is_a: CLCO:0003000 ! has association qualifier

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002004
name: obsolete has negation status
def: "Relates a clinical association to its negation status, indicating whether the asserted relationship is negated." []
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Obsoleted 2026-10-20. Named the axis but not the scope. Because negation (CLCO:0000080) applies at any scope, an assertion through this property discarded the scope, and the same annotation could legitimately be spelled three different ways. The axis is already carried by the value class, so attach negation through the property that commits to a scope." xsd:string
is_obsolete: true
consider: CLCO:0003000, CLCO:0003001, CLCO:0003002

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002009
name: obsolete has uncertainty status
def: "Relates a clinical association to its uncertainty qualifier, indicating that the asserted relationship is uncertain or suspected." []
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Obsoleted 2026-10-20. Named the axis but not the scope. Because uncertainty (CLCO:0000081) applies at any scope, an assertion through this property discarded the scope. The axis is already carried by the value class, so attach uncertainty through the property that commits to a scope." xsd:string
is_obsolete: true
consider: CLCO:0003000, CLCO:0003001, CLCO:0003002

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002100
name: obsolete has participant qualifier
def: "Relates a clinical association to a qualifier that modifies a participant (subject or object) rather than the overall statement or predicate." []
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Obsoleted 2026-10-20. Its domain is the clinical association, so an assertion through this property could not say which participant was qualified, while the definitions of negation and uncertainty both promise a specific subject or object. Split into has subject qualifier (CLCO:0003001) and has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002)." xsd:string
is_obsolete: true
consider: CLCO:0003001, CLCO:0003002

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002500
name: has association participant
def: "Relates a clinical association to a clinical entity that participates in it as either the subject or the object." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES: \"The patient has pneumonia\", \"The MRI showed a mass\", \"Surgery was recommended\" all contain clinical association participants.\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES: \"patient\" alone, \"pneumonia\" alone, and \"quickly\" do not assert an association participant.\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: In \"The patient has pneumonia\", the association has participants patient and pneumonia; in \"The MRI showed a mass\", it has MRI and mass; in \"Surgery was recommended\", it has surgery." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Analogous to RO:0000057 (has participant) but not declared as a sub-property because RO:0000057 relates a process (occurrent) to a continuant, whereas CLCO clinical associations are reified information content entities (subClassOf IAO:0000030), not processes. CLCO uses a statement reification pattern (n-ary relation) in which subject and object slots connect an association class to the entities it asserts a relationship between. This pattern has no direct equivalent in RO, which models relations as direct object properties between BFO-typed instances." xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso RO:0000057

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002501
name: has object
def: "Relates a clinical association (an asserted statement) to the entity that occupies the object position in that association." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES: In \"The patient has pneumonia\", pneumonia is the object; in \"The patient received antibiotics\", antibiotics is the object; in \"The pain is severe\", severe is the object.\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES: patient, received, and the are respectively subject, predicate, and determiner rather than objects.\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: Record OBJECT pneumonia for \"The patient has pneumonia\", OBJECT antibiotics for \"The patient received antibiotics\", and OBJECT severe for \"The pain is severe\"." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "No direct RO equivalent exists. This property fills the object slot in a reified clinical statement (n-ary relation pattern). RO models relations as direct object properties, not as reified statements with named participant slots. See parent property CLCO:0002500 for further rationale." xsd:string
is_a: CLCO:0002500 ! has association participant

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002502
name: has subject
def: "Relates a clinical association (an asserted statement) to the entity that occupies the subject position in that association." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES: In \"The patient has pneumonia\", patient is the subject; in \"The MRI showed a mass\", MRI is the subject; in \"The pain is severe\", pain is the subject.\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES: pneumonia, mass, and severe are objects in those statements, not subjects.\nCONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: Record SUBJECT patient, MRI, and pain for the three corresponding statements above." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "No direct RO equivalent exists. This property fills the subject slot in a reified clinical statement (n-ary relation pattern). RO models relations as direct object properties, not as reified statements with named participant slots. See parent property CLCO:0002500 for further rationale." xsd:string
is_a: CLCO:0002500 ! has association participant

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002603
name: has temporal frame
def: "Relates a clinical association to its temporal frame value (historical, current, future, or hypothetical) indicating when the association holds relative to the clinical document." []
xref: biolink:temporal_context_qualifier
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The patient had pneumonia last year.\"\nSOURCE: \"pneumonia\" => finding\nTARGET: \"last year\" => temporal frame\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\n\"The patient will undergo surgery tomorrow.\"\nSOURCE: \"surgery\" => intervention\nTARGET: \"tomorrow\" => temporal frame\nRELATION: SOURCE => has temporal frame => TARGET\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLE:\n\n\"The patient has had headaches for three weeks.\"\n\"three weeks\" describes duration, NOT the document-relative temporal frame." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Not a sub-property of RO:0002222 (temporally related to) because RO temporal relations use Allen interval algebra to order two occurrents (processes) relative to each other, whereas CLCO temporal frame is a categorical document-relative qualifier (historical/current/future/hypothetical) attached to a reified information entity. The RO_0001900 (temporal interpretation) annotation is retained to indicate that this property has temporal semantics." xsd:string
property_value: RO:0001900 RO:0001901
property_value: seeAlso RO:0002222
range: CLCO:0000082 ! temporal frame
is_a: CLCO:0003000 ! has association qualifier

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0002604
name: has completion status
def: "Relates a clinical association to its workflow completion status (pending, in_progress, or completed). Orthogonal to temporal frame and intention." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The CT results are pending.\"\nSOURCE: \"CT results\" => finding\nTARGET: \"pending\" => completion status\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\n\"The biopsy was completed.\"\nSOURCE: \"biopsy\" => intervention\nTARGET: \"completed\" => completion status\nRELATION: SOURCE => has completion status => TARGET\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLE:\n\n\"The patient will undergo a biopsy.\"\n\"will undergo\" indicates intention or future temporal frame, NOT completion status." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Not a sub-property of has_temporal_context because completion status is not a temporal concept. A pending process may be temporally past (labs drawn yesterday, results pending)." xsd:string
property_value: RO:0001900 RO:0001901
range: CLCO:0000063 ! completion status
is_a: CLCO:0003000 ! has association qualifier

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0003000
name: has association qualifier
def: "Relates a clinical association to a qualifier that modifies the entire assertion rather than one of its participants, such as intention, recommendation, or completion status." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLE:\n\n\"The physician recommended a biopsy.\"\nSOURCE: \"biopsy\" => intervention\nTARGET: \"recommended\" => recommended\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\n\"The patient intends to begin physical therapy.\"\nSOURCE: \"physical therapy\" => intervention\nTARGET: \"intends\" => intention\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\n\"The CT results are pending.\"\nSOURCE: \"CT results\" => finding\nTARGET: \"pending\" => pending\nRELATION: SOURCE => has association qualifier => TARGET\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The patient's mother has breast cancer.\"\nUse: has subject qualifier or has object qualifier for a qualifier modifying a participant, NOT has association qualifier.\n\n\"The patient reported pain in his left knee.\"\nUse: has subject qualifier or has object qualifier for a qualifier modifying a participant, NOT has association qualifier.\n\n\"The patient has had headaches for three weeks.\"\nUse: has temporal frame or a duration representation as appropriate, NOT has association qualifier for the time expression alone.\n\nUse a specific subproperty when one exists, such as has intention, has recommended, or has completion status. These four axes apply only to the whole assertion. For negation and uncertainty, which may apply at any scope, choose has association qualifier, has subject qualifier or has object qualifier according to what the qualifier modifies." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Renamed from \"has statement qualifier\" on 2026-10-20. A clinical association is the reified statement, so statement scope and association scope are the same scope; the two properties were axiomatically identical and have been collapsed into this one. The label \"has association qualifier\" was carried by CLCO:0002000 until 2026-10-20; label-based lookups from before that date resolve to the grouping property, not to this one." xsd:string
range: CLCO:0000067 ! qualifier
is_a: CLCO:0002000 ! has qualifier

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0003001
name: has subject qualifier
def: "Relates a clinical association to a qualifier that modifies the entity filling its has subject slot, rather than the assertion as a whole or the entity filling its has object slot." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"Possible pneumonia was treated with antibiotics.\"\nSOURCE: \"pneumonia\" => finding\nTARGET: \"Possible\" => uncertainty\nRELATION: SOURCE => has subject qualifier => TARGET\nThe treatment did happen; only the diagnosis is uncertain. Attaching the uncertainty to the whole\nstatement would wrongly say the treatment may not have happened.\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The patient was possibly treated with antibiotics elsewhere.\"\nUse: has association qualifier. Here the treatment itself is what is uncertain.\n\n\"The patient will start chemotherapy.\"\nUse: has intention. Intention, recommended and completion status are statement-only axes and are\noutside the range of this property." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-20, replacing has participant qualifier (CLCO:0002100), whose domain is the association and which therefore could not say which participant was qualified. Range is restricted to negation (CLCO:0000080) and uncertainty (CLCO:0000081), the two axes whose definitions state that they apply at any scope. Follows the same convention as SNOMED CT \"Subject relationship context\" and the Biolink subject_/object_ qualifier slots, which both identify the participant role in the attribute name." xsd:string
is_a: CLCO:0002000 ! has qualifier

[Typedef]
id: CLCO:0003002
name: has object qualifier
def: "Relates a clinical association to a qualifier that modifies the entity filling its has object slot, rather than the assertion as a whole or the entity filling its has subject slot." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "POSITIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"Tenderness is present, but not in the right upper quadrant.\"\nSOURCE: \"tenderness\" => finding\nTARGET: \"not\" => negation\nRELATION: SOURCE => has object qualifier => TARGET\nThe finding is asserted; only the site is negated.\n\nNEGATIVE EXAMPLES:\n\n\"The patient denied having a fever.\"\nUse: has association qualifier. The whole assertion is negated, not one participant.\n\n\"The biopsy was completed.\"\nUse: has completion status. Completion status is a statement-only axis and is outside the range of\nthis property." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Added 2026-10-20, replacing has participant qualifier (CLCO:0002100), whose domain is the association and which therefore could not say which participant was qualified. Range is restricted to negation (CLCO:0000080) and uncertainty (CLCO:0000081), the two axes whose definitions state that they apply at any scope. Follows the same convention as SNOMED CT \"Subject relationship context\" and the Biolink subject_/object_ qualifier slots, which both identify the participant role in the attribute name." xsd:string
is_a: CLCO:0002000 ! has qualifier

